{"scenario":"dts-arq-ack-offset","rows":["C-0174","C-0195","C-0212","C-0215","C-0219","C-0220","C-0221","C-0222","C-0223","C-0225","C-0227","C-0233","C-0234","C-0235","C-1150","C-1151","C-1154","C-0213","C-0367","C-0887","C-0886","A-0321","C-0426","C-1260"],"source":"Ed4 C.4.5.5, pp.C-31 to C-32","description":"An acknowledgement too long for one small ACK-ONLY is split into ACK-ONLY D_PDUs with offsets 0 to 7, each Ack Data at most 32 bytes, which together cover the window.","config":{"local_address":"0.0.1.2","csma":{"mode":"jitter"},"modem":{"preamble_ms":600,"flush_ms":150,"waveforms":[{"wn":2,"interleaver":"long","block_bytes":25,"block_ms":4800}]},"cas":{"max_links":4,"link_request_timeout_ms":60000,"link_request_retries":2,"first_data_timeout_ms":120000},"dts":{"ack_wait_ms":60000}},"note":"Conn 1 binds SAP 9 for ARQ. Link setup as cas/make-called-accept and dts-arq/rx-data-acked: at 2000 the peer 0.0.1.3 calls with an Ed4 PHYSICAL LINK REQUEST, recorded Ed4 (B-0408), our accept goes out at 52000 (25 bytes, a whole block, so no fill), and when that transmission ends at 57550 the link is made with the 16-bit family, RX LWE 0 (C-0782). At 61000 one burst from the peer, every D_PDU with EOT 20 (end by 71000): FSN 1 and every eighth FSN from 8 to 2048, so the window from FSN 1 to RX UWE 2048 has 2048 bits, one in eight set after the first. FSN 1 is a whole C_PDU 'ping' without DELIVER IN ORDER, so it is delivered at once (C-0179): cas.first_data stops (B-0215) and the SIS hands it to conn 1. Every other D_PDU is a one-byte middle segment (neither C_PDU START nor END), stored and not delivered. FSN 0 never arrives, so RX LWE stays 0 (C-0776) and an acknowledgement is owed (C-0174). The burst ends at 62000: csma.vdcd_end to 71000, LBT rule 1 (K-0067), contention 12000 ms. At 83000 the acknowledgement goes: for the whole window the bitmap would take 256 bytes (C-0227) and the run length encoding 513 (a code for each single one, for the six zeros after the first and for each later run of seven zeros), both above the 32 bytes this node allows in one ACK-ONLY to keep it small (C-0213; Ed4 C.4.5.5, p.C-31). So the window is split at multiples of 256 FSNs (C-0222, C-1151): each ACK-ONLY covers the most whole 256-FSN units from its offset whose more compact encoding fits 32 bytes, here one unit each, a 32-byte bitmap, since the run length encoding of a unit takes 64 bytes (65 for the first) and two units need 64 bytes either way. So eight ACK-ONLY D_PDUs go, at Offsets 0 to 7, each covering 256 bits (Offset k covers FSN 256 k + 1 to 256 k + 256, C-0233: first bit at RX LWE + 1 + k x 256), every bitmap byte 80 hex except the first, 81. All have RX LWE 0 and Encoding 0 and are in the long form, h = 10 with the Ack Data and a CRC-32 after the header CRC (C-0219, C-0220, C-0234, C-0235): 51 bytes each, from blocks 0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12 and 14 of 17 (EOT 164, 145, 126, 106, 87, 68, 49, 30). Together they acknowledge every D_PDU received (C-0215). Fill (C-1154): the 408 bytes leave 17 in the last block, too few for a copy of a 51-byte ACK-ONLY, so one PADDING D_PDU follows (11 bytes, EOT 10, the peer being recorded Ed4, C-0367, C-0887) and 6 bytes are zero filled. The transmission is 419 bytes, 17 blocks, and ends at 165350; no data of ours, so no dts.ack_wait. Fixture: preamble 600, flush 150, 25 bytes and 4800 ms a block, so an n-block transmission lasts 750 + 4800 n ms, and the EOT of a D_PDU starting in block b of n is ceil((4800 (n - b) + 150) / 500) (C-0104, C-1043). Addresses 0.0.1.2 (this node) and 0.0.1.3 take address size 3 (C-0133), so a DATA-ONLY is 19 bytes plus its segment, an ACK-ONLY 15 bytes plus its Ack Data in the header form and 19 bytes plus its Ack Data and CRC-32 in the long form, a PADDING D_PDU 11 bytes. Seed 0 draws uniform(16) = 15, 4, 15, 12: contention waits 45000, 12000, 45000, 36000 ms (K-0080).  The SIS soft link times are unset, so they are derived: sis.soft_link_idle and sis.soft_link_min_hold (called node only) three answer waits, sis.soft_link_max six; none falls due within the run, and the idle wait stops while an ARQ U_PDU is outstanding (A-0320, A-0321, A-0326). Since corpus 0.28.0 (P7-3), every D_PDU this node sends to a peer recorded Ed4 carries EOW 0xF01, CAPABILITY (Ed4 1, Duplex 0), where it carried EMPTY (C-0426, C-1260); an owed UNRECOGNIZED-TYPE-ERROR still goes first (C-1079), and D_PDUs to a peer of unknown edition, a peer recorded Ed3 or a group carry EMPTY as before. Where this note says EOW 0 or EMPTY for such a D_PDU, read CAPABILITY. Only EOW and header CRC bytes changed."}
